---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The Journaling Mastermind — The Soul Mami" description="A monthly journaling mastermind with Eliana Reyes — first Sunday of every month. Pen, paper, good company, and your own inner voice.">

  <!-- Beat: Invitation -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">First Sunday · Monthly</span>
        <h1>The Journaling <em class="soul">Mastermind</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Once a month, we gather with pens, paper, and zero
          performance. You'll write your way underneath the noise and
          meet what's actually true for you — in the company of people
          doing the same.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <!-- TODO: replace with real signup/checkout link from Eliana -->
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/lets-talk/">Save my seat</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#how">How it works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img class="photo photo--arch" src="/images/circle-rest.jpg" alt="Circle members resting close together on blankets, smiling" fetchpriority="high" style="max-height:460px;" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Reality -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why Journaling</span>
      <h2>Your inner voice isn't gone. It's buried.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Under the to-do lists, the roles, the shoulds, and everyone
        else's opinions, there's a voice that knows exactly who you are
        and what you need. Journaling is the shovel.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alone, most of us journal for three days and quit — or circle
        the same page of surface thoughts. In a circle, with real
        prompts and real humans, something else happens. You go
        deeper, you stay honest, and you keep coming back. That's the
        mastermind part: we hold each other to our own depth.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Process -->
  <section class="section" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose center" style="margin-inline:auto;">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Flow</span>
        <h2>What a Sunday looks like</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="step-num">01</span>
          <h3>We land</h3>
          <p>We arrive, breathe, and drop out of the week's noise together. No performing, no small talk required.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="step-num">02</span>
          <h3>We write</h3>
          <p>I guide you through prompts built around the month's theme — know yourself, be with yourself, live as yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="step-num">03</span>
          <h3>We share</h3>
          <p>Only what you want, only if you want. Being witnessed is medicine; so is witnessing. You leave lighter, clearer, and more you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- TODO: session length, time zone, location (virtual/in-person), price, and platform details from Eliana -->
      <p class="center muted" style="margin-top:2rem;">First Sunday of every month. Full details land in your inbox when you join the garden or reach out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Proof -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose center" style="margin-inline:auto;">
        <span class="eyebrow">From the Circle</span>
        <h2>What people say after they write</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <figure class="card quote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>"Everything! Eliana holds such an excellent space for meaningful journaling. What keeps bringing me back is the community. There is so much respect, wisdom, and equal opportunity to connect, express, share and collect insights that inspire and motivate me. I really value these monthly sessions and wouldn't change a thing."</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Circle member</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>"Thank you all for being here to co-create this beautiful and safe space, especially to Eliana for hosting it. This nurtures me throughout the month."</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Circle member</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>"I love all the prompts from this recent journal session. Thank you so much for the invite, and the facility for souls to be nourished."</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>Circle member</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Questions -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2>Wondering…</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to be "a writer"?</summary>
        <p>Nope. If you can hold a pen and tell yourself the truth, you're qualified. Grammar is not invited to this circle.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I don't want to share out loud?</summary>
        <p>Then you don't. Sharing is always an invitation, never a requirement. Some of the deepest sessions are the quietest ones.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I've never journaled consistently. Is this still for me?</summary>
        <p>Especially for you. The circle is the consistency. You just have to show up one Sunday a month — the momentum takes care of itself.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What do I need to bring?</summary>
        <p>A notebook, a pen you like, and whatever's true for you that day. That's the whole kit.</p>
      </details>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/lets-talk/">Save my seat</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/garden/">Get the next invite by email</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--honey);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand-deep);
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
  }
  summary {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--espresso);
  }
  details p { margin-top: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
</style>
